#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/059_the_canoe_race/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Race us! Whoever touches the jetties of Ålberga, Dimmberga and Svanetorp first and comes back here"
" wins. Can you do it before the day ends?"
msgstr "우리랑 경주해요! 올베랴, 딤베랴, 스바네토르프의 선착장을 먼저 찍고 여기로 돌아오는 쪽이 이겨요. 해가 지기 전에 할 수 있겠어요?"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/059_the_canoe_race/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ålberga: touched! The canoe is right behind you!"
msgstr "올베랴, 찍었어요! 카누가 바로 뒤에 있어요!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/059_the_canoe_race/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Dimmberga! Row, row, they are close!"
msgstr "딤베랴! 저어요, 저어요, 바짝 쫓아와요!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/059_the_canoe_race/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Svanetorp! Now back to Kråkhamn!"
msgstr "스바네토르프! 이제 크로크함으로 돌아가요!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/059_the_canoe_race/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You won! But only by a nose. Next time we win! Here, the prize: a honey cake each, and silver."
msgstr ""
"이겼어요! 그런데 아슬아슬했어요. 다음엔 우리가 이길 거예요! 자, 상품이에요. {crew|꿀 케이크 하나랑|꿀 케이크 하나랑|꿀 케이크 하나씩이랑|꿀 케이크 하나씩이랑} "
"은화예요."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/059_the_canoe_race/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Vikings loved contests: rowing, swimming, wrestling and running."
msgstr "바이킹은 노 젓기, 헤엄치기, 씨름, 달리기 같은 시합을 좋아했어요."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
