#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/096_the_winter_stores/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Autumn again! Before the lakes freeze, fill the store: ten crates of hay and six of grain, within "
"three days. You know how by now!"
msgstr "또 가을이구나! 호수가 얼기 전에 창고를 채우자. 사흘 안에 건초 열 상자와 곡식 여섯 상자란다. 이제 어떻게 하는지 알지!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/096_the_winter_stores/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hay for all our animals. Now the grain."
msgstr "우리 동물들 모두 먹을 건초로구나. 이제 곡식이야."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/096_the_winter_stores/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The store is full to the roof! Not one animal will be hungry this winter."
msgstr "창고가 지붕까지 꽉 찼구나! 올겨울엔 배고픈 동물이 하나도 없을 거야."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/096_the_winter_stores/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Autumn was the busiest time: everything for the long winter had to be in."
msgstr "가을은 가장 바쁜 때였어요. 긴 겨울을 날 것을 모두 들여놓아야 했거든요."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/097_fish_for_every_farm/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Fish for Every Farm"
